Javier,

Having empty lines within the tps file is not a problem. I just confirmed this using readland.tps() and a file with spaces in between specimens. So something else is amiss for your example.

As for the code you sent, one thing I noticed was your line:

Mouse2d<-two.d.array(mouse)

Since mouse has only 1 specimen, this will create a p*k vector, not a p x k matrix.  It is still a matrix in the sense of R, but not how you are envisioning it.  Just do:

Mouse2d<-mouse[,,1]

Then the rest of your downstream code might make some sense (I did not confirm this however).

Dean

